<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<odoo>
    <!--
        No domain: every contact takes part, children included.

        That is safe only because the engine refuses to pair records under
        different parents, in SQL, unconditionally. Without that guard this
        would be actively harmful: contacts attached to a company are
        routinely named after a ROLE rather than a person — every company has
        an "Accounts Payable", a "Reception", a "Comptes payables" — and those
        fold to an identical deduplication key while being entirely different
        people at entirely different companies. Measured on a real database of
        ~36k partners, of which ~81% were child contacts, comparing across
        parents produced single groups of 811, 729 and 596 records consisting
        purely of role names.

        With the guard in place the two useful comparisons both happen and the
        harmful one cannot: companies and standalone individuals compare among
        themselves (NULL parent matches NULL parent), and children compare
        only with their own siblings.
    -->
    <record id="dedup_target_partner_name" model="bemade.dedup.target">
        <field name="model_id" ref="base.model_res_partner" />
        <field name="field_id" ref="field_res_partner__dedup_key" />
        <field name="domain">[]</field>
    </record>
</odoo>
